From: alioth iOS bring-up 2026-10-24
Subject: [PATCH] work_interval: soft-fail a second CA_CLIENT interval

This tree is compiled with -DXNU_TARGET_OS_OSX, so the non-app half of
native-work-interval-soft-fail is already active here (work_interval.c:1053)
and needs no change. The other half is missing: a task that already holds a
CA_CLIENT work interval gets KERN_FAILURE, and UIKit takes that as a
programming error and aborts the process.

Mark the interval IGNORED instead, which is exactly what the non-app path
does: the caller presses the buttons and the interval is simply not connected
to anything.

--- a/osfmk/kern/work_interval.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/work_interval.c
@@ -1066,7 +1066,13 @@
 #endif /* XNU_TARGET_OS_OSX */
 		}
 		if (task_set_ca_client_wi(creating_task, true) == false) {
-			return KERN_FAILURE;
+			/*
+			 * A second CA_CLIENT interval in one task is accepted but
+			 * left unconnected, the same way the non-app case above
+			 * soft-fails. UIKit creates one per task and treats a
+			 * refusal as a programming error.
+			 */
+			create_flags |= WORK_INTERVAL_FLAG_IGNORED;
 		}
 	}
 
